{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>And if your brother grows poor, etc.</b> This passage alludes to what they said, of blessed memory, in the Zohar (Tikkunim 10): that HaShem commanded the prince of Edom — who is Samael — not to behave with cruelty toward Israel. And this is the meaning of His saying <b>if your brother grows poor</b>, after the manner of what it says (Malachi 1:2): ״הֲלֹא אָח עֵשָׂו לְיַעֲקֹב״. ״עִמָּךְ״ — meaning, his decline and poverty is on account of his being ״with you,״ for he cleaved to your evil ways. <b>And he be sold to you</b>, after the manner of (Isaiah 52:3): ״חִנָּם נִמְכַּרְתֶּם״, and they interpreted in the Zohar (II 128a) that the aspect of Samael is called חִנָּם, for the exile of this host is to Edom — ״Remember, HaShem, the children of Edom.״" "And HaShem commands: <b>you shall not make him serve the service of a slave</b>, after the manner of what it says (Jeremiah 2:14): ״הַעֶבֶד יִשְׂרָאֵל״ etc. — rather, <b>as a hired worker, as a sojourner he shall be</b> etc. This is because there are two aspects in Israel: the multitude of the people, and ״they that sit at the table, the men of wisdom״ (II Samuel 23:8). And you will find that even though Israel are subject to taxes and imposts, Torah scholars are not included, as it is written (Deuteronomy 33:3): ״וְהֵם תֻּכּוּ לְרַגְלֶךָ״, and they said, of blessed memory (Bava Batra 8a) etc., and it is written (Ezra 7:24): ״מִנְדָּה בְלוֹ וַהֲלָךְ לָא שַׁלִּיט״ etc. Corresponding to the multitude of the people He said ״as a hired worker,״ for they are sold on account of their sins, and corresponding to the righteous He said ״as a sojourner,״ for they are merely sojourning among the nations in exile but no royal burden is upon them." "And His saying <b>until the Jubilee year</b> — this is the boundary of redemption, as is known; ״he shall serve with you,״ and HaShem informs that in the end he will depart from him, as it is written <b>and he shall go out from being with you</b>, <b>he and his children</b> — meaning, the sparks that are refined through their being with him, and this is the sod of the exile. For if not so, why would HaShem not chastise them with the rod of chastisement there, in their land and in their inheritance? Rather, one of the reasons is in order to refine the holy sparks from among the lands, for in every place where Israel are found, through the sufferings and the Torah and the commandments, the sparks are refined of themselves; and this is the sod of what it says (Ecclesiastes 8:9): ״עֵת אֲשֶׁר שָׁלַט הָאָדָם בְּאָדָם לְרַע לוֹ״." "And if you would say: if so, had Israel not sinned and gone into exile, who would have refined the sparks that are now refined through the dispersion of Israel? Know that if Israel had not sinned, they would have had the power to refine the holy sparks in the place where they are, from all the places they would have come to — which is not so after their sin, which weakened their power, so that they can barely reach the place itself where the sparks are." "And He said <b>and he shall return to his family</b>: for when the Redeemer comes, HaShem will implant His light, may He be blessed, among us — where the family of the nation of Israel is. Also, those who dwell in the dust will arise, and each man will return to the inheritance of his fathers; it is the everlasting light, the Holy Temple established by His hands, may He be blessed." "<b>You shall not rule over him with rigor, and you shall fear your Elohim</b> — and from this aspect he incurs a death penalty at the hands of Heaven, as they said, of blessed memory (Sukkah 52b), for he has acted with hubris and transgressed the commandment of HaShem."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {5 "The Hebrew reads מוּתְרֶה which appears to be a typographical variant or error for מוּתְרַד (the Aramaic technical term for execution by Heaven, corresponding to סמא״ל); rendered according to context following the cited Talmudic passage."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:01:43.698830489Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}